 Focus on advanced retrieval techniques like hybrid search and re-ranking (e.g., Cohere) to reduce agent hallucinations.\\n* **Evaluation & Observability:** Learn how to debug and trace non-deterministic agent outputs using tools like LangSmith or Phoenix by Arize.\\n\\n### 3. Projects to Build\\n* **Project 1: Autonomous Research & Writing Team (Multi-Agent):** Build a system using CrewAI or LangGraph featuring a \"Researcher Agent\" that scrapes the web, a \"Fact-Checker Agent\" that validates sources, and a \"Writer Agent\" that compiles a polished report with human-in-the-loop approval before final export.\\n* **Project 2: RAG-Powered Customer Support Agent with Memory:** Build a LangGraph agent connected to a vector database containing product documentation. Implement persistent memory so the agent can handle multi-turn troubleshooting and escalate to a human when confidence is low.\\n\\n### 4. Job-Readiness Actions\\n* **Build a \"Proof-of-Work\" Portfolio:** Record 60-second video Loom demos of your multi-agent projects actually running (showing tool calls, errors, and self-corrections) and pin them to your GitHub repository READMEs.\\n* **Contribute to Open Source:** Fix issues or add documentation to popular agentic repositories (e.g., LangChain, LangGraph, CrewAI) to signal real-world collaboration skills.\\n* **Target the Right Roles:** Look for titles like *AI Engineer*, *LLM Application Engineer*, or *Automation Engineer (AI)* in startups and innovation teams that are actively building production-grade agent workflows.', 'extras': {'signature': 'EmAKXgFpFH0TVu1FjUM/osTpg++dNmOuVXCWvGqK74w59XbIMehhgS1PKY78zSkEDA7A9sShdruR47aBMF46GHNovGZIqAgALbVP6uvgT0ZfFgwjS2c6pYS5gE7ciTTWNOo='}}]\n","\n","✓ Profile intake completed\n","✓ Career analysis completed\n","✓ Skill gap analysis completed\n","✓ Career roadmap completed\n","✓ Shared state preserved across all stages\n","✓ Full Career Copilot workflow passed\n","\n","Phase 4 Cell 11 Complete\n"]}],"source":["# ==